==English==

===Etymology===
From the slogan “New Labour, New Britain”, used by {{w|Tony Blair}} in his 1994 Labour Party Conference speech.<ref>
{{cite-web
|year=1994
|month=October
|author=Tony Blair
|authorlink=Tony Blair
|title=Leader's speech, Blackpool 1994
|work=British Political Speech
|url=http://www.britishpoliticalspeech.org/speech-archive.htm?speech=200
|passage=The next election will offer us the chance to change our country, not just to promise change, but to achieve it - the historic goal of another Labour government. Our party - new Labour; our mission - new Britain. New Labour, new Britain.}}</ref>

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[new|New]] [[Labour]]}}

# {{lb|en|UK politics}} A [[movement]] in the 1990s and 2000s to [[rebrand]] the [[British]] [[Labour Party]] by [[discarding]] [[traditional]] [[goal]]s such as [[nationalization]] and [[socialism]].

